===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|of a person|predicative|_|only}} [[angry|Angry]], [[distressed]]{{,}} or [[unhappy]].
#: {{ux|en|He was '''upset''' when she refused his friendship.}}
#: {{ux|en|My children often get '''upset''' with their classmates.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=05 Dec 81|volume=9|number=20|journal=Gay Community News|page=9|author=Jana Runnals;Rosemary Schonfeld|title=The Liberalisation of 'Women's Music'|text=We were shocked when we asked a disruptive man in the front row to move to the back, and when he subsequently left, the producer's helpers were so '''upset''' for him they gave him two free tickets to the next 'women's music' production.}}
# {{lb|en|of a [[stomach]] or [[gastrointestinal tract]]}} Feeling unwell, nauseated, or ready to [[vomit]].
#: {{ux|en|His stomach was '''upset''', so he didn't want to move.}}
#: {{ux|en|Bryan came home from school with an '''upset''' tummy.}}

