===Noun===
{{wikipedia|upset|upset (unexpected victory)}}
{{wikipedia|aircraft upset}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} {{cap|disturbance}} or [[disruption]].
#: {{ux|en|My late arrival caused the professor considerable '''upset'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|sports|politics}} An unexpected [[victory]] of a competitor or candidate that was not favored to win.
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=January 8, 2011
|author=Paul Fletcher
|title=Stevenage 3 - 1 Newcastle
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/fa_cup/9341905.stm
|page=
|passage=But it is probably the biggest '''upset''' for the away side since Ronnie Radford smashed a famous goal as Hereford defeated Newcastle 2-1 in 1972.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=March 9, 2016
|author=Harry Enten
|title=What The Stunning Bernie Sanders Win In Michigan Means
|work=FiveThirtyEight
|url=http://fivethirtyeight.com/features/what-the-stunning-bernie-sanders-win-in-michigan-means/
|page=
|passage=Sanders’s win in Michigan was one of the greatest '''upsets''' in modern political history.}}
# {{lb|en|automobile insurance}} An [[overturn]].
#: ''"collision and '''upset'''": impact with another object or an overturn for whatever reason.''
# An [[#Adjective|upset]] [[stomach]].
#* '''1958''' May 12, advertisement, ''Life'', volume 44, number 19, page 110&nbsp;[http://books.google.com/books?id=vFMEAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA110&dq=pepto]:
#*: "Bob, let's cancel the babysitter. With this upset stomach, I can't go out tonight.
#*: "Try Pepto-Bismol. Hospital tests prove it relieves '''upsets'''. And it's great for indigestion or nausea, too!"
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} An [[upper set]]; a [[subset]] (X,≤) of a [[partially ordered]] [[set]] with the property that, if x is in U and x≤y, then y is in U.
# {{lb|en|aviation}} The dangerous situation where the flight attitude or airspeed of an aircraft is outside the designed bounds of operation, possibly resulting in loss of control.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Civil Aeronautics Board|title=Aircraft Accident Report: Northwest Airlines, Inc., Boeing 720B, N724US, Near Miami, Florida, February 12, 1963|url=https://rosap.ntl.bts.gov/view/dot/33689|accessdate=25 November 2022|date=1 June 1965|chapter=Synopsis|page=1|text=The Board determines that the probable cause of this accident was the unfavorable interaction of severe vertical air drafts and large longitudinal control displacements resulting in a longitudinal '''upset''' from which a successful recovery was not made.}}
# {{lb|en|basketry}} A [[woven]] [[row]] supporting the [[foundation]] [[rod]]s for the [[upright]]s of a [[basket]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1972|author=Nilima Roy|title=Basketry and Mat-weaving in India
|passage=Willow basket making, an artisan inserting bye-stakes in the '''upsets'''.}}

